%N A400906 Irregular triangle: n-th row is the prime factorization of the first n digits of Pi.
%H A400906 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="/A400906/b400906.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1277</a>
%H A400906 Hisanori Mishima, WIFC (World Integer Factorization Center), <a href="https://www.asahi-net.or.jp/~kc2h-msm/mathland/matha1/de_pi000.htm">Decimal expansions of Pi (n = 0 to 100)</a>.
%e A400906 Triangle begins:
%e A400906   3;
%e A400906   31;
%e A400906   2, 157;
%e A400906   3, 3, 349;
%e A400906   5, 61, 103;
%e A400906   314159;
%e A400906   ...
%t A400906 row[n_]:=Flatten[ConstantArray@@@FactorInteger[Floor[Pi*10^n]]]; Array[row, 18, 0] // Flatten (* _Stefano Spezia_, Oct 11 2026 *)
